      "writtenOn": "2025-01-14T13:17:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Are the mappable extended buffers always allocated in that memory heap? We should double check that as there could be a mappable but not coherent / cached / host visible heap as well.",
      "revId": "aff981a64c5ed478a15b96fab10782f6a2ccee7a",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e17086f5_45d32398",
        "filename": "src/dawn/native/vulkan/PhysicalDeviceVk.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 472,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000019
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-01-15T08:05:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "No. Only readable mapping needs `VK_MEMORY_PROPERTY_HOST_CACHED_BIT` for the maximum performance of the memory read on CPU side. Now if the mapping is not readable we won\u0027t allocate memory on that memory heap.",
      "parentUuid": "41d0b610_8f405fc6",
      "revId": "aff981a64c5ed478a15b96fab10782f6a2ccee7a",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c686d97d_94d575c3",
        "filename": "src/dawn/native/vulkan/PhysicalDeviceVk.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 472,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000002
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-01-15T13:10:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We need the `CACHED` bit on `MapWrite` memory as well as much as we can IIRC, or use non-temporal write assambly instructions (which applications won\u0027t). I can\u0027t find the link again, but otherwise we might need to do loads all the way from memory to combine them with the write in some cases. Causing huge slowdowns.",
      "parentUuid": "e17086f5_45d32398",
      "revId": "aff981a64c5ed478a15b96fab10782f6a2ccee7a",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
